This thesis presents a baseline measurement with the STAR detector of neutral pion and eta meson production in \(p+p\) and \(d+\mathrm{Au}\) collisions at a center-of-mass energy of \(\sqrt{s_{NN}}=200\;\mathrm{GeV}\). The neutral pion spectrum complements that of the charged pions measured in STAR in the range \(0.35<p_{T}<10\;\mathrm{GeV}\!/c\)[28] and extends up to \(p_{T}=17\;\mathrm{GeV}\!/c\). Preliminary results of this analysis have been published in [29, 30]. Also presented in this thesis are the first measurements by STAR of \(\eta\) meson production.

