The second significant source of neutral clusters in the calorimeter are the neutral hadrons produced in the collision, mostly antineutrons. As a first attempt to account for the additional low mass background from these hadrons, simulations of antineutrons were performed in the same way as photons and the reconstructed invariant mass distribution was added according to the realistic proportion \(\bar{n}/\gamma=\bar{n}/2\pi^{0}\). The ratio \(\bar{n}/\pi^{0}\) was taken to be equal to the average value of \(\bar{p}/\pi^{-}\) from the STAR measurement [28] in the \(p_{T}\) range covered by each of MinBias and HighTower datasets. In the bottom plot of Figure 5.10 we compare the simulated low mass background (histogram) to the data.

